If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use then it is possible that a ten-percent-of-original-dose-per-week-or-slower-first-taper-stage succeeds for the patient.
If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use and the patient reaches an approximately-thirty-percent-of-original-dose then it is possible that a clinician decreases a remaining-opioid-dose by an approximately-ten-percent at an interval of 1 week for the patient.
A shorter-opioid-use-duration-example is a weeks-to-months-duration-example.
